CM_ "FusionPilot: the rear radar DIGEST -- the contract between the feeder microcontroller and openpilot.";
CM_ BO_ 1600 "Nearest CLOSING target on the left, already reduced from 64 raw detections at 33 Hz. Sent at 20 Hz.";
CM_ BO_ 1601 "Nearest CLOSING target on the right. Same layout as left deliberately, so one decoder serves both.";
CM_ BO_ 1602 "Feeder and sensor health. RearApproach must read this before believing a quiet bus means a clear road.";
CM_ SG_ 1600 DRel "Distance BEHIND the car, positive rearward. 0.25 m resolution is well inside what a 3 s TTC gate needs.";
CM_ SG_ 1600 VRel "Positive = CLOSING on us, matching RearApproachSide.from_radar. Stated because ESR.dbc and ford_fusion_2018_adas.dbc disagree on sign for the same hardware.";
CM_ SG_ 1600 YRel "Lateral offset, left positive. Sent so the LANE BINNING stays tunable in software -- the feeder must not own a threshold nobody can change without reflashing.";
CM_ SG_ 1600 TargetCount "How many closing targets this side had. Zero with Detected set is impossible and means a feeder bug.";
CM_ SG_ 1602 DetectionHz "Measured rate of MRR_Detection frames the feeder is seeing. Falls to 0 if the radar dies, which a silent digest alone cannot distinguish from an empty road.";
